  == Veg Gravy ==

Heat @ghee{2%tablespoons} in a #kadai{} or pan. Add the @tej patta{1}(Indian bay leaf), @cloves{2}, @cinnamon{1%inch}, @black cardamoms{2}, @mace flower{1} and @green cardamoms{2}, and let them splutter and become aromatic.

Add @onions{3/4%cup}(thinly sliced) and sauté till golden.

Add @ginger-garlic paste{1%teaspoon} and sauté for a few seconds.

Add @chopped mix veggies{2 - 2.5%cups}(carrots, potato, cauliflower, capsicum, french beans, mushrooms) and @green peas{1/3%cup}, and stir well.

Add @red chili powder{1%teaspoon} and @garam masala powder{1%teaspoon}, and mix well.

Keep heat low and add @fresh curd{1/4%cup}(yogurt), mixing well.

Add @water{1%cup}, season with salt, and cover the pan to simmer until veggies are cooked.

== Rice ==

In a #bowl{}, soak @sella basmati rice{1.5%cups} for ~{1%hour}.

Soak @saffron strands{1%pinch} in @warm milk{1/3%cup} for ~{15-20%minutes}.

Heat @water{5 to 6%cups} with @salt{1%teaspoon}, @tej patta{1}(Indian bay leaf), @green cardamoms{2}, @cinnamon{1/2%inch} and @cloves{2}.

Bring water to boil, add soaked rice, and cook until ¾th done.

== Assembly ==

Drain 75% cooked rice and layer it with the prepared veg gravy.

Pour saffron-infused milk over rice and add @stock{1/3%cup}.

Add @kewra water{2%teaspoons} or @?rose water{}, and dot with @ghee{1/2 to 1%tablespoon}.

Seal the pan with #aluminum foil{} and cover with the #lid{}.

Cook on low heat for ~{30-35%minutes} or bake at 180 degrees Celsius for the same time.

== Garnish ==

Fry @onions{1/2%cup}(thinly sliced) in @ghee{1%tablespoon} until golden.

Let the biryani stand for ~{7-10%minutes} after cooking, then serve hot or warm garnished with fried onions and @?mint leaves{}.